{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>He shall not take.</b> He has no act of taking with her, and kiddushin do not take effect with her (cf. Kiddushin 67)." "<b>And he shall not uncover his father's wing.</b> His father's yevamah who is fit for his father — and he has already been warned concerning her under ״עֶרְוַת אֲחִי אָבִיךָ״ (Leviticus 18). Rather, it is to transgress this one in two negative commandments, and to adjoin to it ״לֹא יָבֹא מַמְזֵר,״ to teach that a mamzer results only from those liable to karet — and all the more so from those liable to court-imposed death, for there is no prohibited relation subject to court-imposed death that does not also carry karet (Yevamot 49)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:04.498026331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}